WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:04.840
Too many Californians are out of work or in jobs that don't support a family,

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.050
while too many businesses have good jobs they can't fill.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.490
And California is many economies.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.700
In the same year, unemployment in one part of the state

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.150
runs nearly five times the rate in another.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.200
In a state this diverse, only local business and community leaders

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.080
can know which investments will arm workers with the skills to fill good jobs

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.330
and build a strong local economy.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.200
Those leaders serve on California's 45 local workforce development boards.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:34.760
Nearly a thousand members, appointed by local elected officials

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:35.950
and led by business.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.100
Together, the boards serve every community in California.

00:00:40.256 --> 00:00:43.446
This is California's workforce development infrastructure.

00:00:44.456 --> 00:00:48.956
Nearly 50,000 Californians who left these programs earned $1.26 billion

00:00:48.976 --> 00:00:50.386
the following year.

00:00:50.576 --> 00:00:56.786
That is $3.72 in wages for every federal Title I dollar local boards received.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.950
AI is beginning to change what many jobs require,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.480
and new federal work requirements

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.050
are expected to send more people looking for work.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.950
Neither will arrive the same way in every community.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.450
Local boards see the change in their own communities

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.500
and adjust their investments to meet it.

00:01:12.053 --> 00:01:14.283
Through the California Workforce Association,

00:01:14.513 --> 00:01:17.243
our member boards put new policy and funding to work,

00:01:17.513 --> 00:01:19.133
learn from areas like their own,

00:01:19.153 --> 00:01:22.523
and bring what local leaders know to Sacramento and Washington.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:26.400
As new leaders take office in Sacramento and Washington,

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:27.600
our message is this.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.550
Invest in the infrastructure California already has.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.400
Trust local leaders to decide.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:33.800
Hold them to results.

00:01:36.015 --> 00:01:38.205
The California Workforce Association.
